846:% First suppose that $\{\vec{0}\}\cup B\cup -B$ is a 2-blocking set. Note that every $x\in C$ is of the form $x=u^\transp G$ for some $u\in \F_3^k$. 
848:% Therefore, to show that $C$ is a trifferent code, it suffices to show that for any three distinct $u,v,w\in \F_3^k$ there is a $b\in B$ such that $u^\transp b$, $v^\transp b$ and $w^\transp b$ are distinct. 
855:% Now suppose that $C$ is a trifferent code. 
